cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper (preferred-citation) and the repository."
type: software
title: "PGMN: Physics-Guided Mixture Density Network for temporally continuous reconstruction of satellite soil moisture"
abstract: >-
  MATLAB implementation and reproduction package for PGMN, a physics-guided
  residual-learning framework that reconstructs temporally continuous SMAP
  surface soil moisture on the EASE-Grid 2.0 Global 36 km grid. An open-loop
  water balance model driven by precipitation alone provides the baseline, and
  a mixture density ConvLSTM predicts the distribution of the baseline
  residual; the reconstruction is the baseline minus the predicted residual,
  and every value carries a predictive standard deviation. The repository
  ships one 64 x 64 patch over the central United States with the trained
  model for that patch, so the evaluation-period accuracy and the calibration
  diagnostics reported in the paper can be reproduced from MATLAB in under a
  minute.
